-- title:
--   Toric points are m-torsion in Pic⁰
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, with residue field of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed. Let $\Lambda$ be a datum `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM A` (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` compatible with the generic point, together with a scheme with relative group law over `base p` and identifications of its generic and special fibre points with the level-$(M/p)$ points and with $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduction), and let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`, i.e. a smooth separated quasi-compact surjective group scheme over `base p` with commutative relative group law, Galois-equivariant identification of its generic-fibre sections with `JH M H`, Hecke correspondences and the further structure recorded in that definition. Then, for every natural number $m$, the subgroup `O.toricPts m` of `JH M H` — which is trivial when $m = 0$ and otherwise is generated by the range of the toric point map `O.toricPoint m hm` — is contained in the $m$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$ inside Laurent series, where $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ is the group of degree-zero divisors supported on places modulo principal divisors and its $m$-torsion is the $\mathbb{Z}$-torsion by $m$.
--
--   This is the torsion half of the analysis of the toric part of the $m$-torsion of a semi-abelian Néron model at a prime dividing the level: the toric points constructed from characters of the character group of the toric part are killed by $m$. It is used in the description of the finite and toric parts of the $m$-torsion of the level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ Néron object, notably in [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_toricFiniteFiltration_tateModule_jH_self`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_toricFiniteFiltration_tateModule_jH_self) and [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.mem_toricPts_iff_exists_fibreMap_abqFibre_eq_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.mem_toricPts_iff_exists_fibreMap_abqFibre_eq_one).
